The ReSTIR story's one-dimensional example of bias
==================================================

What the story draws on the canvas (lab/src/math/) for chapter 6's beats `c6-1d` and `c6-fix`: the paper's Fig. 7
redrawn from the lab's runs of it (demos/bias.rs): the target ramp, the flat and the step distributions, the true
inverse of RIS's output density (the thick line), and the mean of W (the thin line), as `biasReveal` draws them,
for the candidates, weight, and step of `biasCandidates`, `biasWeight`, and `biasNearZero`, with a marker at
`biasMark`. Beside the plot, one stage per sentence of the two beats as its stage (`stepOf "bias" 31`, the clips below) goes from 0 to 31: what the
lines are, the count W divides by, Eq. 19, the fix, the near-zero step's huge weights, the balance heuristic, and
Talbot's weight, whose cost the grid of every candidate and every distribution shows.

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* render_lab_math]
$[Import* paper_restir_values]
$[Import* paper_restir_natives]
$[Import* paper_restir_common]

The layout

The plot's box, the right column's centre, and the size of its formulas.
$[# _plotBox [% {box {v2 -6.6 -2.6} {v2 0.6 2.8}}]]
$[# _rightX 4.1]
$[# _size 0.44]
The rows of the right column: the legend's, then three for what each sentence adds.
$[# _slotB 0.5]
$[# _slotC -0.8]
$[# _slotD -2.1]
The step's colour, beside the flat distribution's (`pColor`), and the two lines'.
$[# _stepColor [% {rgb "#b48cff"}]]
$[# _truthColor [% {rgb "#6be3b0"}]]
$[# _meanColor [% {rgb "#ffa14a"}]]

Fn([String, String, Color, Float, Bool], List(Mob)). A legend row at height y: a swatch of the curve's colour,
thick or thin, and its formula beside it.
$[# {_legend id latex color y thick}
    [# swatch {line {++ id "Swatch"} {v2 1.7 y} {v2 2.3 y} color {!if thick 6.0 2.5}}]
    {append swatch {nextTo {tex id latex 0.42 color} swatch right 0.2}}]

The plot

Fn([List(Float), Float], Float). Per-bin values read at `x` (0 to 1): between the two bins' middles around it,
linearly (held at the first and last bins' outside them).
$[# {_valueAt values x}
    [# n {length values}]
    [# f {clamp {- {* x {float n}} 0.5} 0.0 {float {- n 1}}}]
    [# i {min {floor f} {- n 2}}]
    {lerp {nth values i} {nth values {+ i 1}} {- f {float i}}}]
Fn([Axes, List(Float), Float, Color, Float], List(Mob)). A curve of per-bin values drawn as far as `upTo` across,
each value at its bin's middle (clamped to the plot's top).
$[# {_binned id ax values upTo color width}
    [# n {length values}]
    [# first {/ 0.5 {float n}}]
    [# points {filter
        {map
            {zip {range 0 n} values}
            {^ {e} {v2 {/ {+ {float {.first e}} 0.5} {float n}} {min 4.0 {.second e}}}}}
        {^ {p} {<= {.x p} upTo}}}]
    {!if {< upTo first}
        {'}
        {pathThrough id
            {map
                {append points {' {v2 upTo {min 4.0 {_valueAt values upTo}}}}}
                {^ {p} {onAxes ax {.x p} {.y p}}}}
            color
            width}}]
Fn([Float, Float, Float], {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}). The two lines for `count`
candidates, the weight, and the step's floor `near`: those for the whole counts on either side, the weights on
either side, and the step zero or nearly zero past one half, blended (a growing count, a changing weight, or a
rising floor moves the lines, never jumps them). A whole value is read once.
$[# {_curvesAt count weight near}
    [# {_mix xs ys u} {map {zip xs ys} {^ {e} {lerp {.first e} {.second e} u}}}]
    [# {_blend a b u} {pair {_mix {.first a} {.first b} u} {_mix {.second a} {.second b} u}}]
    [# {_lines m w z} [# c {biasCurves m w z}] {pair {.meanW c} {.truth c}}]
    [# {_over x f}
        [# lo {floor x}]
        [# u {- x {float lo}}]
        {!if {< u 0.0001} {f lo} {_blend {f lo} {f {+ lo 1}} u}}]
    [# f {smooth {phase near 0.3 0.7}}]
    [# {_atFloor z} {_over {max count 1.0} {^ {m} {_over weight {^ {w} {_lines m {float w} z}}}}}]
    [# lines {!if {< f 0.0001}
        {_atFloor 0.0}
        {!if {> f 0.9999} {_atFloor 1.0} {_blend {_atFloor 0.0} {_atFloor 1.0} f}}}]
    {:
        {.
            meanW {.first lines}
            runs {.runs {biasCurves {max 1 {floor count}} weight 0.0}}
            truth {.second lines}}
        {Struct {' {Field "meanW" {List Float}} {Field "runs" Int} {Field "truth" {List Float}}}}}]

Fn([Float, Float], Float). How far `reveal` has gone into curve `n` (0 to 1).
$[# {_upTo reveal n} {clamp {- reveal n} 0.0 1.0}]
Fn([Float, Float], Float). The opacity of what curve `n` brings once it is drawn: in over the next 0.8 of `reveal`.
$[# {_shown reveal n} {smooth {phase reveal n {+ n 0.8}}}]

Fn([Axes, Float, Float, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). The plot: the axes, then
each curve as far as `reveal` has drawn it (the target, the flat PDF, the step, the thick line, the thin line).
$[# {_plot ax reveal near c}
    [# {_curve id f n color width} {!if {< {_upTo reveal n} 0.01}
        {'}
        {plot id ax f 0.0 {_upTo reveal n} color width}}]
    {flatten {'
        {axesFigure "axes" ax textDimColor 0.34 true true}
        {_curve "target" biasTarget 0.0 targetColor 3.0}
        {_curve "flat" {^ {x} {biasPdf 0 x near}} 1.0 pColor 2.5}
        {_curve "step" {^ {x} {biasPdf 1 x near}} 2.0 _stepColor 2.5}
        {_binned "truth" ax {.truth c} {_upTo reveal 3.0} _truthColor 7.0}
        {_binned "mean" ax {.meanW c} {_upTo reveal 4.0} _meanColor 2.5}}}]
Fn([List(Float), Float], Float). Per-bin values near `x`, averaged over a few bins around it: a dot riding a line
slides down its cliffs and over its noise rather than dropping in one frame.
$[# {_valueNear values x} {/
    {fold {' -0.04 -0.02 0.0 0.02 0.04} 0.0 {^ {t d} {+ t {_valueAt values {+ x d}}}}}
    5.0}]
Fn([Axes, Float, Float, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). The marker at the value
`set` (at the story's first place, 0.05, while it is not set: the score fades it in and out), with the two lines'
values on it once they are drawn.
$[# {_marker ax reveal set c}
    [# mark {max set 0.05}]
    {flatten {'
        {line "marker" {onAxes ax mark 0.0} {onAxes ax mark 4.0} accentColor 2.5}
        {faded
            {dotAt "markTruth"
                {onAxes ax mark {min 4.0 {_valueNear {.truth c} mark}}}
                0.1
                _truthColor}
            {_shown reveal 3.6}}
        {faded
            {dotAt "markMean"
                {onAxes ax mark {min 4.0 {_valueNear {.meanW c} mark}}}
                0.08
                _meanColor}
            {_shown reveal 4.6}}}}]

Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The legend, each row fading in as its curve is drawn.
$[# {_legends reveal} {flatten {'
    {faded {_legend "lTarget" f"{\hat p(x) = 2 - 2x}" targetColor 3.15 false} {_shown reveal 0.0}}
    {faded {_legend "lFlat" f"{p_1}" pColor 2.65 false} {_shown reveal 1.0}}
    {faded {_legend "lStep" f"{p_2}" _stepColor 2.15 false} {_shown reveal 2.0}}
    {faded
        {_legend "lTruth" f"{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}" _truthColor 1.65 true}
        {_shown reveal 3.0}}
    {faded {_legend "lMean" f"{\overline{W}(x)}" _meanColor 1.15 false} {_shown reveal 4.0}}}}]

What each sentence adds

Fn([Float, Float, Float, Float], List(Mob)). The candidates in a row at slot C: the flat ones and the step ones (as
many as `count`, the last fading in as the count grows past it), the step ones struck out where the marker is past
the step (they cannot produce y; struck as the marker passes the step, unless the step has a floor), at the
strike's progress `t`, and the count that could.
$[# {_candidates t count mark near}
    [# m {round count}]
    [# shown {max 1 {ceil count}}]
    [# could {+ {div m 2} {!if {> {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near} 0.0} {div m 2} 0}}]
    [# {_x i} {+ {- _rightX {* 0.13 {- count 1.0}}} {* 0.26 {float i}}}]
    [# dots {flatten {map
        {range 0 shown}
        {^ {i} {faded
            {dotAt f"{cand${str i}}"
                {v2 {_x i} {+ _slotC 0.35}}
                0.09
                {!if {= {% i 2} 0} pColor _stepColor}}
            {clamp {- count {float i}} 0.0 1.0}}}}}]
    [# steps {map {filter {range 0 shown} {^ {i} {= {% i 2} 1}}} {^ {i} f"{cand${str i}}"}}]
    [# blocked {* {smooth {phase mark 0.48 0.52}} {- 1.0 {smooth {phase near 0.0 0.2}}}}]
    [# struck {crossParts {* t blocked} dots steps accentColor}]
    {append struck {moveTo
        {tex "could" f"{|Z(y)| = ${str could} \quad M = ${str m}}" _size textColor}
        {v2 _rightX {- _slotC 0.35}}}}]

Fn([Float, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). At the marker: the two lines' values
there and their ratio.
$[# {_atMarker mark c}
    [# bins {length {.truth c}}]
    [# bin {clamp {floor {* {max mark 0.0} {float bins}}} 0 {- bins 1}}]
    [# truth {nth {.truth c} bin}]
    [# mean {nth {.meanW c} bin}]
    {moveTo
        {texParts "atMark" f"{\lit{1}{\overline{W}} \cdot \lit{2}{p} = \frac{${numberLatex mean 2}}{${numberLatex truth 2}} = ${numberLatex {over mean truth} 2}}" _size textColor
            {' "W" "p"}
            {' _meanColor _truthColor}}
        {v2 _rightX _slotD}}]

Fn([Float, Float], List(Mob)). Talbot's cost at slot C and D: a grid of every candidate (rows) and every
distribution (columns) as `count` grows (the new row and column fading in), all lit, then only the kept sample's row
lit (the paper's weight), with their counts.
$[# {_grid s count}
    [# nf {max count 2.0}]
    [# n {ceil nf}]
    [# cell {/ 2.4 nf}]
    [# x0 {- _rightX 1.2}]
    [# y0 {- _slotC 0.2}]
    [# one {smooth {phase s 30.0 30.6}}]
    [# cells {flatten {map
        {range 0 {* n n}}
        {^ {k}
            [# r {div k n}]
            [# col {% k n}]
            [# lit {!if {= r 0} 1.0 {- 1.0 {* 0.85 one}}}]
            [# grown {clamp {- nf {float {max r col}}} 0.0 1.0}]
            {filled f"{cell${str r}.${str col}}"
                {box
                    {v2 {+ x0 {* cell {float col}}} {- y0 {* cell {float {+ r 1}}}}}
                    {v2 {+ x0 {* cell {+ {float col} 0.85}}} {- y0 {* cell {+ {float r} 0.15}}}}}
                {!if {= r 0} accentColor targetColor}
                {* {* 0.8 lit} grown}}}}}]
    [# m {round count}]
    [# total {moveTo
        {tex "gridCount" f"{n^2 = ${str {* m m}}}" _size textColor}
        {v2 {- _rightX 2.3} {- y0 1.2}}}]
    [# single {moveTo
        {tex "gridCount" f"{n = ${str m}}" _size textColor}
        {v2 {- _rightX 2.3} {- y0 1.2}}}]
    {append cells {transform {phase s 30.0 30.6} total single}}]

The scene

Fn([Float, Float, Float, Float, Float], Score). The 1D example as a score of 31 steps, read with the bias values
(the candidates `count`, the weight, the step's floor `near`, how far the curves are drawn `reveal`, and the marker
`mark`): the plot and its legend, the marker, and what each sentence adds beside the plot.
$[# {_score count weight near reveal mark}
    [# c {_curvesAt count weight near}]
    [# ax {axesIn _plotBox {axisRange 0.0 1.0 0.25} {axisRange 0.0 4.0 1.0}}]
    [# {_at y fig} {moveTo fig {v2 {min _rightX {- 6.9 {/ {widthOf fig} 2.0}}} y}}]
    [# {_rule id latex names colors} {_at _slotB {texParts id latex _size textColor names colors}}]
    [# {_still fig} {^ {s} fig}]
    [# {_point ids} {^ {t f} {pointParts t f ids accentColor}}]
    [# {_shownOver id fig from to} {part id fig {'
        {enterOver from 0.5 fadeIn}
        {exitOver {- to 0.4} 0.4 fadeOut}}}]
    [# runs {flatten {'
        {_at _slotB {tex "runsF" f"{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}" _size _truthColor}}
        {_at _slotC {tex "runsN" f"{${str {.runs c}}}" _size textColor}}
        {_at {- _slotC 0.55} {caption "runsNote" {textKey "biasmath-runs"} 0.32 textDimColor}}}}]
    [# huge {_at _slotD {tex "huge" f"{w = \frac{\hat p(y)}{p_2(y)} = \frac{${numberLatex {biasTarget {max mark 0.0}} 2}}{${numberLatex {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near} 4}} = ${short {over {biasTarget {max mark 0.0}} {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near}}}}" _size
        textColor}}]
    {score "bias" 31
        {'
            {part "plot" {_still {_plot ax reveal near c}} {' {enterOver 0.0 0.8 fadeIn}}}
            {part "legend" {_still {_legends reveal}} {'}}
            {part "marker"
                {_still {_marker ax reveal mark c}}
                {' {enterOver 3.5 0.2 fadeIn} {exitOver 22.8 0.2 fadeOut}}}
            {_shownOver "leftHalf"
                {_still {filled "leftHalf"
                    {box {onAxes ax 0.0 0.0} {onAxes ax 0.5 4.0}}
                    _truthColor
                    0.22}}
                8.0
                9.0}
            {_shownOver "rightHalf"
                {_still {filled "rightHalf"
                    {box {onAxes ax 0.5 0.0} {onAxes ax 1.0 4.0}}
                    pColor
                    0.22}}
                9.0
                10.0}
            {_shownOver "runs" {_still runs} 5.0 7.0}
            {_shownOver "should"
                {_still {_rule "should" f"{\lit{1}{\overline{W}(x)} = \lit{2}{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}}"
                    {' "W" "p"}
                    {' _meanColor _truthColor}}}
                7.0
                9.5}
            {part "divides"
                {_still {_rule "divides" f"{W = \frac{\sum w_i}{\lit{1}{M}\,\hat p(y)}}"
                    {' "M"}
                    {' accentColor}}}
                {'
                    {enterOver 10.0 0.5 fadeIn}
                    {emphasize 10.4 11.0 {^ {t f} {pointParts t f {' "M"} targetColor}}}
                    {exitOver 11.6 0.4 fadeOut}}}
            {_shownOver "candidates"
                {^ {s} {_candidates {phase s 10.4 11.0} count mark near}}
                10.0
                13.0}
            {_shownOver "atMarker" {_still {_atMarker mark c}} 11.0 15.4}
            {part "eq19"
                {_still {_rule "eq19" f"{E[W \mid y] = \frac{1}{p(y)} \cdot \frac{\lit{1}{|Z(y)|}}{\lit{2}{M}}}"
                    {' "Z" "M"}
                    {' accentColor accentColor}}}
                {'
                    {enterOver 12.0 0.5 fadeIn}
                    {emphasize 13.0 14.0 {^ {t f} {pointParts t f {' "Z" "M"} targetColor}}}
                    {exitOver 16.6 0.4 fadeOut}}}
            {_shownOver "darkNote"
                {_still {moveTo
                    {caption "darkNote" {textKey "sourcemath-dark"} 0.32 _meanColor}
                    {onAxes ax 0.75 4.45}}}
                14.0
                15.4}
            {_shownOver "neighbourNote"
                {_still {moveTo
                    {caption "neighbourNote" {textKey "biasmath-neighbour"} 0.32 _stepColor}
                    {onAxes ax 0.4 4.45}}}
                15.0
                17.0}
            {part "fix"
                {_still {_rule "fix" f"{W = \frac{\sum w_i}{\lit{1}{|Z(y)|}\,\hat p(y)}}"
                    {' "Z"}
                    {' accentColor}}}
                {'
                    {enterOver 17.0 0.5 fadeIn}
                    {emphasize 19.0 20.0 {^ {t f} {pointParts t f {' "Z"} targetColor}}}
                    {exitOver 22.6 0.4 fadeOut}}}
            {_shownOver "candidatesFix"
                {^ {s} {_candidates {phase s 17.4 18.0} count mark near}}
                17.0
                22.0}
            {_shownOver "huge" {_still huge} 22.0 23.0}
            {part "balance"
                {_still {_rule "balance" f"{m_i(y) = \frac{p_i(y)}{\lit{1}{\sum_j p_j(y)}}}"
                    {' "sum"}
                    {' pColor}}}
                {'
                    {enterOver 23.0 0.5 fadeIn}
                    {emphasize 24.0 25.0 {_point {' "sum"}}}
                    {exitOver 26.6 0.4 fadeOut}}}
            {_shownOver "balanceNote"
                {_still {append
                    {_at _slotC {caption "balanceNote" {textKey "biasmath-balance"} 0.32 textColor}}
                    {_at
                        {- _slotC 0.45}
                        {caption "balanceNoteMis"
                            {textKey "biasmath-balance-mis"}
                            0.32
                            textColor}}}}
                25.0
                27.0}
            {part "talbot"
                {_still {_rule "talbot" f"{w_i = \frac{\hat p(x_i)}{\lit{1}{\sum_j p_j(x_i)}}}"
                    {' "sum"}
                    {' pColor}}}
                {' {enterOver 27.0 0.5 fadeIn}}}
            {part "grid" {^ {s} {_grid s count}} {' {enterOver 28.0 0.5 fadeIn}}}}
        {'}}]

The hook

Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The 1D example at stage its stage (`stepOf "bias" 31`, the clips below).
$[# biasMath {: {^ {t} {playScore {_score
    {biasCandidates}
    {biasWeight}
    {biasNearZero}
    {biasReveal}
    {biasMark}}}} Math}]

Clips

The scene's steps as clips (lab/src/clip.rs): its demonstration's Play plays every step in order, a second each,
and moves the bias values (how far the curves are drawn, the marker, the candidates, the weight, the step's floor)
as the story does; the story plays each step over its sentence's words, and sets the scene back to a step where a
beat starts.
$[# biasSteps [% {together {'
    {stepsInOrder "bias" 31}
    {clip {'
        {keys "biasReveal" {map
            {'
                {pair 0.0 0.0}
                {pair 1.0 0.0}
                {pair 2.0 1.0}
                {pair 3.0 2.0}
                {pair 4.0 3.0}
                {pair 5.0 4.0}
                {pair 6.0 4.0}
                {pair 7.0 5.0}}
            {^ {k} {keyframe {.first k} {.second k} "linear"}}}}
        {keys "biasMark" {map
            {'
                {pair 0.0 -1.0}
                {pair 3.49 -1.0}
                {pair 3.5 0.05}
                {pair 4.0 0.45}
                {pair 8.0 0.45}
                {pair 9.0 0.05}
                {pair 10.0 0.9}
                {pair 11.0 0.6}
                {pair 13.0 0.6}
                {pair 14.0 0.75}
                {pair 15.0 0.75}
                {pair 16.0 0.2}
                {pair 17.0 0.55}
                {pair 18.0 0.9}
                {pair 22.0 0.9}
                {pair 23.0 0.6}
                {pair 23.01 -1.0}}
            {^ {k} {keyframe {.first k} {.second k} "smooth"}}}}
        {keys "biasCandidates" {map
            {'
                {pair 0.0 2.0}
                {pair 4.0 2.0}
                {pair 5.0 4.0}
                {pair 6.0 6.0}
                {pair 7.0 10.0}
                {pair 11.0 10.0}
                {pair 12.0 20.0}
                {pair 16.0 20.0}
                {pair 17.0 4.0}
                {pair 21.0 4.0}
                {pair 22.0 10.0}
                {pair 26.0 10.0}
                {pair 27.0 14.0}
                {pair 29.0 14.0}
                {pair 30.0 20.0}}
            {^ {k} {keyframe {.first k} {.second k} "linear"}}}}
        {keys "biasWeight" {map
            {' {pair 0.0 0.0} {pair 18.0 0.0} {pair 19.0 1.0} {pair 23.0 1.0} {pair 24.0 2.0}}
            {^ {k} {keyframe {.first k} {.second k} "linear"}}}}
        {keys "biasNearZero" {map
            {' {pair 0.0 0.0} {pair 20.0 0.0} {pair 21.0 1.0}}
            {^ {k} {keyframe {.first k} {.second k} "linear"}}}}}}}}]]
$[# biasAt0 [% {stepsAt "bias" 31 0}]]
$[# biasAt17 [% {stepsAt "bias" 31 17}]]
$[# biasStep1 [% {stepClip "bias" 1 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep10 [% {stepClip "bias" 10 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep11 [% {stepClip "bias" 11 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep12 [% {stepClip "bias" 12 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep13 [% {stepClip "bias" 13 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep14 [% {stepClip "bias" 14 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep15 [% {stepClip "bias" 15 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep16 [% {stepClip "bias" 16 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep17 [% {stepClip "bias" 17 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep18 [% {stepClip "bias" 18 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep19 [% {stepClip "bias" 19 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep2 [% {stepClip "bias" 2 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep20 [% {stepClip "bias" 20 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep21 [% {stepClip "bias" 21 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep22 [% {stepClip "bias" 22 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep23 [% {stepClip "bias" 23 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep24 [% {stepClip "bias" 24 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep25 [% {stepClip "bias" 25 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep26 [% {stepClip "bias" 26 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep27 [% {stepClip "bias" 27 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep28 [% {stepClip "bias" 28 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep29 [% {stepClip "bias" 29 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep3 [% {stepClip "bias" 3 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep30 [% {stepClip "bias" 30 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep31 [% {stepClip "bias" 31 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep4 [% {stepClip "bias" 4 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep5 [% {stepClip "bias" 5 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep6 [% {stepClip "bias" 6 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep7 [% {stepClip "bias" 7 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep8 [% {stepClip "bias" 8 0.0 1.0}]]
$[# biasStep9 [% {stepClip "bias" 9 0.0 1.0}]]
